(version 1)

# 24-pin ATX daughterboard -- 10 blade-tab joints (12V x1 / 5V x2 / 3.3V x2 / 5VSB x1 / GND x4; iteration-7 count at the TE 63969-1 receptacle's 22.9A rating under the ratified 125% policy) + a 1x4 blind-mate signal stub (-12V/PS_ON#/PWR_OK/GND), standing perpendicular to the main board, tabs blade-down per the owner's 2026-07-05 sketch, dropping into TE 63969-1 FASTON PCB receptacles (hole pair perpendicular to the row, memo addendum 7). Power netclass 0.5mm/0.9-0.5mm via matches the 0.5mm stub tracks laid by route_atx24(); each of the 4 bus rails also gets its own thin In2.Cu lane zone in the corridor below the field (0.3mm wide, 0.65mm pitch -- not netclass-controlled, drawn directly; see ATX24_LANE_SLOT), which the tab row's down-stubs and the field's dodge-stubs meet through 0.3/0.5mm vias.

(rule "Power min width"
	(constraint track_width (min 0.4mm))
	(condition "A.NetClass == 'Power'"))
